  "notes": "Headless syringe dispense PASS/FAIL: the packet must exit the housing and be presented, and the housing must not move. Events packet_exit and packet_presentation and checks exactly_one_packet and pickup_ready come from the frozen acceptance.toml (raw SHA256 518a45ffc4592ca602be4c33c59681038e43dedaa15b688312202c3a57ff6ca2) via dispense3_acceptance.json, every number unchanged. Housing thresholds are copied from s0_acceptance.json (raw SHA256 150c037b2e985dac46b66670c46291872d9e0cc9d287d7946eadf4d9185b5a3a): the body_pose_retained max and max_rotation_rad, the body_drop signed world-z lower and upper, and the penetration bound and validity. Pose and drop are checked with window=max_over_phase in each of actuate, press_hold, release and hold. Binding changes from the frozen documents, and the only ones: (1) packet_exit and packet_presentation bodies are [packet, packet_02, packet_03], the 3-packet identity list of pocky_dispense3_v1 (extended, never narrowed). (2) packet_presentation support_bodies is [housing] instead of the frozen [lip, body]: this design has no lip or body bodies, and the housing is the one-piece lip plus body, so this is an identity binding, not a threshold change. (3) The S0 body/chassis pose and drop checks are bound to housing against floor_world: pose is housing vs floor_world with the S0 body_pose_retained thresholds (not the looser chassis_grounded 1 mm); drop is the signed world-z translation of housing relative to floor_world from initial, with the S0 body_drop bounds. (4) The S0 contact_duration checks against pusher, rod and crank (body_on_*, lip_on_*) are omitted because those bodies do not exist in the syringe; the slider is the actuated part and is not required to be unloaded. No settled-speed checks are carried over, as in pocky_dispense3_v1. Expected outcome is not asserted before the run.",
